+Feature: TodoMVC Application
+  As a user
+  I want to manage a todo list
+  So that I can track tasks I need to complete
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  @logic
+  Scenario: App hides main and footer when there are no todos
+    Then the "#main" element should not be visible
+    And the "#footer" element should not be visible
+
+  @logic
+  Scenario: User creates a new todo by pressing Enter
+    When the user types "Buy milk" into the ".new-todo" input
+    And presses Enter
+    Then a todo item with the title "Buy milk" appears in the ".todo-list"
+    And the ".new-todo" input is cleared
+
+  @logic
+  Scenario: App ignores empty and whitespace-only input
+    When the user types "   " into the ".new-todo" input
+    And presses Enter
+    Then no new todo item is added
+
+  @logic
+  Scenario: User marks a todo as completed
+    Given a todo item with the title "Buy milk" exists
+    When the user clicks the todo's toggle checkbox
+    Then the todo's "<li>" has the class "completed"
+    And the todo's toggle checkbox is checked
+
+  @logic
+  Scenario: Mark-all-as-complete toggles all todos
+    Given todo items with the titles "Buy milk" and "Write code" exist
+    When the user clicks the "#toggle-all" checkbox
+    Then all todo items have the class "completed"
+
+  @logic
+  Scenario: Mark-all-as-complete reflects individual toggles
+    Given todo items with the titles "Buy milk" and "Write code" exist
+    When the user marks the first todo as completed
+    And the user marks the second todo as completed
+    Then the "#toggle-all" checkbox is checked
+
+  @logic
+  Scenario: User clears completed todos
+    Given completed todo items exist
+    When the user clicks the ".clear-completed" button
+    Then no todo items have the class "completed"
+
+  @logic
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when no completed todos
+    Given a todo item exists that is not completed
+    Then the ".clear-completed" button should not be visible
+
+  @logic
+  Scenario: User edits a todo title on double-click
+    Given a todo item with the title "Buy milk" exists
+    When the user double-clicks the todo's label
+    Then the todo's "<li>" has the class "editing"
+    When the user sets the edit input value to "Buy oat milk" and presses Enter
+    Then the todo item has the title "Buy oat milk"
+    And the todo's "<li>" does not have the class "editing"
+
+  @logic
+  Scenario: Editing and pressing Escape discards changes
+    Given a todo item with the title "Buy milk" exists
+    When the user double-clicks the todo's label
+    And the user presses Escape during editing
+    Then the todo item has the title "Buy milk"
+    And the todo's "<li>" does not have the class "editing"
+
+  @logic
+  Scenario: Editing an empty title destroys the todo
+    Given a todo item with the title "Buy milk" exists
+    When the user double-clicks the todo's label
+    And the user clears the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo item with the title "Buy milk" does not exist
+
+  @logic
+  Scenario: Counter displays the number of active todos
+    Given todo items exist with 2 active and 1 completed
+    Then the ".todo-count" element contains "<strong>2</strong> items left"
+
+  @logic
+  Scenario: Routing filters the todo list by route
+    Given todo items exist with 1 active and 1 completed
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then only the active todo items are visible in the ".todo-list"
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then only the completed todo items are visible in the ".todo-list"
+    When the user navigates to "#/"
+    Then all todo items are visible in the ".todo-list"
+
+  @logic
+  Scenario: Active filter link has the selected class
+    Given the app is loaded
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the filter link for "Active" has the class "selected"
+    And the other filter links do not have the class "selected"
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the filter link for "Completed" has the class "selected"
+    And the other filter links do not have the class "selected"
+
+  @logic
+  Scenario: Active filter persists on reload
+    Given the user navigates to "#/active"
+    When the app is reloaded
+    Then the filter link for "Active" has the class "selected"
+
+  @logic
+  Scenario: Todos persist across reloads via localStorage
+    Given a todo item with the title "Buy milk" exists
+    When the app is reloaded
+    Then a todo item with the title "Buy milk" appears in the ".todo-list"
+
+  @logic
+  Scenario: Editing state is not persisted
+    Given the user double-clicks a todo's label to enter editing mode
+    When the app is reloaded
+    Then no todo item has the class "editing"
\ No newline at end of file
